# The repro scripts under .kiro/specs/distill-contracts/repro are run inside
# Linux containers straight from the checkout. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows
# clone would hand them CRLF, and `sh script.sh` then dies on the literal
# carriage return, so pin LF regardless of the cloning platform.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf

# Go sources are LF in the object store; without this a Windows clone checks
# them out CRLF, and `gofmt -l .` inside a Linux container then flags every file
# on the carriage returns alone — a false CI signal on the local pre-push check.
*.go    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
